WEBVTT

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.440
Aah. I drank too much last night.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.640
My head hurts.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.950
What should I do?

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.970
The more I look at him, the cuter he looks.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.170
Oh shoot, my body's getting so hot.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.630
U-Um...

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.870
Heh. Morning.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.060
Whoa, that was close. I was about to get winged.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.840
Hey, Ashikabi-kun.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:03.910
Y-Yes?

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.740
Your father... What kind of a person is he?

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.880
Father?

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.260
Um, I don't have one.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:18.650
Apparently he's alive, but my mom refuses to tell me anything about him.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.360
I see.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:24.150
You're not winged yet, are you, Kazehana-san?

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.430
Aren't you going to participate in The Sekirei Project?

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.550
There was someone I liked.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.310
But... I was rejected.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.470
Someone you liked?

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.830
Participating in The Sekirei Project without someone I like would be meaningless.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.330
Hey, Ashikabi-kun...

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.230
Y-Yes?!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.720
Don't you want me?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.100
Th-That's...

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.480
What do you...?!

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:17.240
atarashii yakusoku ga kokoro wo tsuyoku tsunagu

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:17.240
Our new promise binds our hearts together strongly

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.330
kawaru sekai ni kane ga hibiku yukou

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.330
The bell rings in the changing world, let's go

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:31.170
owari naki tatakai ga subete wo hiki saitemo

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:31.170
Even if the endless fight shreds everything apart,

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:37.350
kimi no hohoemi tada shinjite

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:37.350
I will believe in your smile

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.560
kimi no yume mamoreru nara

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.560
If I can protect your dream,

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.150
itami sae dakishimeyou

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.150
I will even embrace pain

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:54.450
kasane au kono omoi mune no chikai yuzurenai

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:54.450
I can't let go of these piling feelings, this oath in my heart

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:01.200
aa, sora no haruka hate made

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:01.200
Ah, all the way to the end of the sky,

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:09.420
sou, kakete yuku you na kasoku shiteku jounetsu

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.000
yes, my passion accelerates

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.420
as if it were rushing through my body

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:15.590
aa, donna unmei datte

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:15.590
Ah, no matter what kind of fate awaits me,

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:26.730
sou, takaku koeteku makenai yuuki kureta kara

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.890
yes, I can fly high over it

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:26.730
because you gave me this undefeatable courage

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.920
Second Wing

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.920
The Wind Rises

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.250
Thanks for the food!

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.350
Could you pass me the soy sauce?

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:40.490
Here you go.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.620
Thanks.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.060
Don't you want me?

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.460
Wh-What was that supposed to mean?

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.260
Minato-san, have some veggies.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.050
Say "aah!"

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.450
I'm telling you, I can eat by myself.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:58.110
Even though it's only something like getting home first from shopping...

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.500
Why can't I do it?

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.670
I'm good at running.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.660
I'll beat you next time and steal that seat for myself!

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.910
Hey now...

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.930
Wouldn't it be better to just pick something else to compete in?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.570
That would mean it's my loss!

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.120
A true wife must be able to best any task.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:19.530
Well, now is the only time you can easily get worked up about something like this.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.010
Hey, you! What do you mean "easily"?!

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.790
Tsukiumi, calm down...

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.790
Say, Matsu-san. Did something happen?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.710
The Sekirei that tried to escape was defeated by the Disciplinary Squad.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.620
The Disciplinary Squad?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:39.320
The news about an Ashikabi and a Sekirei that managed to escape have already spread.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.660
Escaped? You mean Shiki-kun and Kuno-san?

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:50.530
The news of their efforts have given other Ashikabi and Sekirei who do not wish to fight a faint hope.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.410
However...

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.050
Nobody has succeeded since then.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:05:03.600
Instead, it spreads deep despair which causes those peace-loving people to get dragged into needless battles.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.100
N-No way...

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.680
That means that every other Sekirei can be considered an enemy, right?

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.360
Just the way I like it.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:11.780
An enemy?

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:12.730
Thanks for the food.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:20.790
What I wanted to say is that you should be careful when you go out.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:26.230
The Demonic Ashikabi and his Grim Reaper Sekirei, who would even mercilessly attack other Ashikabi.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.390
There's one called that, too.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.420
D-Demonic Ashikabi?

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.760
That doesn't sound too good...

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.370
D-Dammit.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.690
I-I remember now!

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:52.040
These two are known as the Demonic Ashikabi and Grim Reaper Sekirei, and they are looking for someone!

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.620
Another dead end, huh?

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:03.370
Kuu...

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.050
It's going to be all right, Shiina.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.460
We'll definitely find her!

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.250
Okay.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:11.940
Yeah.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.640
Oh, Onii-chan!

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.740
Yukari, how are you?

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:20.540
I haven't seen you in a while. I was wondering how you were doing.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.480
I've been pretty busy. Is Musubi-tan doing well?

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.820
She's the same as usual.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.540
Aah, I totally want to grope her boobs again.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.640
Boobs...

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:31.420
Listen, you...

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:35.010
Oh, yeah! Can I come over to play?

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.310
Come here?

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.090
Musubi, be careful.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:42.750
I'll be the one sitting next to Minato during dinner.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:43.920
I won't lose to you!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.960
Oh? You said it.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.450
I'm going to sit next to him again.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.480
How am I going to explain this to her?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.580
What the hell is this?

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.870
Why do you have a flock of women around you?

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:55.770
Is this a harem?

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.000
Or some kind of a VIP club?

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.750
An indecent man-woman relationship?

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:00.470
You're the worst.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:02.720
Hey!

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.010
I can't tell her anything about The Sekirei Project either...

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:04.100
You there?

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:05.460
Are you listening?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:07.830
Onii-chan!

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.480
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.500
Then, would you like to meet somewhere and grab a bite?

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.600
Sure. That sounds good.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.860
All right, in front of the station. Later.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.000
Who did you just talk to, Minato?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.180
Just my little sister!

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:23.950
Little sister?

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:26.910
Ah, Yukari-san. How nostalgic.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.470
Who? You know her?

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.150
Yup. I met her once before.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.670
She's very nice and funny.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.390
I promised to meet her for dinner tonight.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.760
Is that so?

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:42.320
Oh, she was worried about you too, Musubi-chan.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:43.820
Really?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.290
I want to see Yukari-san as well.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.610
Huh? Tsukiumi?

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.510
Cheers.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.520
Looks like someone's in a foul mood,

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.060
Miss "your panties are in full view".

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.290
What are you doing there?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.580
I can't laze around my room, it's too loud.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.220
Sake in the middle of the day is the best.

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:21.800
What do you mean, in the middle of the day? You drink all day long.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.590
You see,

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.920
a long time ago, I was heartbroken.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:26.990
Heartbroken?

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:30.720
I went on a long journey to heal my wounded heart.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.540
But...

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.680
But?

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:38.370
It turned out to be a country-wide sake tour!

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.210
How stupid of me to listen to you seriously.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:50.420
Is that heartbreak of yours the reason why you're not winged yet?

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.390
Who knows?

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:56.210
Maybe I just haven't met a good enough man since then.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.120
I don't get it.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.760
I never thought that way before I met Minato.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.920
No. It was probably because I just hated them all.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.920
But, now you're all lovey-dovey with your Ashikabi-kun.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.800
O-Of course! My feelings for Minato are second to none!

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:12.880
That's all fine, isn't it?

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:16.060
Falling in love has nothing to do with logic,

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.270
Flasher-chan.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.760
You're one to talk!

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:23.470
Also... Don't call me a flasher!

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.600
Yeah. It's not logical at all.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.630
I see. With your little sister.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.710
Yes. So I won't be needing any dinner.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.470
I understand.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.160
Please, take us with you next time.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.450
O-Of course.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.160
Tsukiumi?

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.140
You really don't have to guard me.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:56.070
According to Matsu, I can't let you walk outside alone.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:56.880
But,

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:57.830
I'm going to...

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.510
You're meeting your little sister, aren't you?

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.330
While you're at it, I might as well introduce myself as your true wife.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.070
That could be a little-

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:11.260
Musubi met her. But my - your true wife's - inability to meet your family members is just unfair!

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:13.390
Isn't it, Minato?!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:16.080
Y-Yes! It's exactly as you say!

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:17.850
What the...?

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.020
No. 09 is guarding him?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.950
Well, I have Haihane here with me.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.210
What's the problem?

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:29.420
The last episode of the show I watch is on TV right now.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:32.690
You can just go and get someone to record it for you!

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.160
Kidnapping is a pain.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.830
It would be easier to just take them head on.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:42.770
Do you think that would make me feel better after being humiliated like that?

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:48.120
I need to mentally scar him so bad that it makes him want to cry for his mommy.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:49.480
C'mon, let's go.

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:53.550
TV...

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.070
Move it!

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.790
For the time being, the Capital is divided by

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.100
Higa of the East,

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.150
Sanada of the West,

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.090
Mikogami of the South.

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:03.290
Those are the three major superpowers in equilibrium right now.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.280
How long are they going to be able to maintain this balance?

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.050
Excuse me.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:12.370
Kazehana-tan.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:13.670
What's the matter?

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:16.320
I'm out of sake.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.210
Do you have any?

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.140
What about the pantry?

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:21.580
Miya won't let me.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:25.740
What's that?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.450
Experimental alcohol.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:30.360
Well, it's pure alcohol.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.530
Hey, Tsukiumi.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:33.080
What is it?

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.220
Wouldn't it be better to put off meeting Yukari until next time?

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:41.860
Why do you have to be so hesitant about introducing your wife to your family?!

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:43.190
Th-That's because, you see...

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:45.840
The Sekirei Project and everything else is a secret and all!

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.320
Then you should proudly tell her that I'm your beloved wife.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.300
Well, that's also a bit...

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.350
Step back, Minato!

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.750
Th-The Disciplinary Squad?

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:03.380
No. 104 Haihane.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:04.350
What are you up to?!

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.960
The Disciplinary Squad is also a part of The Sekirei Project.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.200
A-Are you saying that you want to fight?

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.080
So it wasn't a mistake to guard you, after all.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:14.540
Tsukiumi?

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:17.500
I'll gladly accept this challenge!

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.630
No. 09 Tsukiumi,

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:22.160
incoming!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.030
Wait...

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.490
Minato, don't move.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:25.590
Water Arrows!

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:31.440
Are you running away?

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.040
Tsukiumi!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.510
Yo. How have you been?

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:39.630
Another Disciplinary Squad member?!

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.850
It's No. 105 Benitsubasa.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.620
Make sure to remember it well.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:13:00.540
What are you hoping to achieve by running away after challenging me?

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:02.770
Will you fight me fair and square already?

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:10.910
Finally in the mood to fight?

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:15.350
Water Celebration!

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.140
Water Blade!

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:24.860
Water Dragon!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:36.250
You weren't this fast the last time...

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.880
You used Minato as a shield back then, so I couldn't move around freely.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.780
This time's... the same.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:45.630
What?

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:52.010
That's it?

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:58.420
This much should be enough... Probably.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:13:59.950
What do you mean?!

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:00.310
Hey!

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.060
This much?

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:05.410
And it's the same as the last time?

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:06.580
Then...

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:08.940
That time...

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:14.790
Minato!

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:29.810
Where am I?

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:31.800
What's going on?

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:34.930
That's my...!

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:36.650
I'm borrowing this for a second.

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:41.340
Can someone get that?

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:42.140
Okay!

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.040
Hello! Who is it?

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:50.430
Put the big titted woman on the line.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:51.840
Big titted?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.720
Hurry up and put her on the line.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.300
The No. 88!

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:58.150
She's there, isn't she?

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.750
Eighty eight?

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.670
Give me some potatoes and carrots, please!

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:03.380
All right.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:09.350
1, 2, 3, 4, 5...

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.370
Eh? Why are you counting?

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:11.530
Kuu-chan, who's calling?

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.200
Who is it?

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.250
It doesn't matter who I am.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.860
Is she there or not?

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:18.270
I'm right here.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.510
Not you! No. 88!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.590
This really hits the spot.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.520
Who would've thought that you'd actually drink it.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:30.740
Rather, you're going to get sick.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.020
Eighty eight?

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.810
Kusano-tan, who's on the phone?

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:35.970
Who is it?

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:39.030
I just said, it doesn't matter who I am!

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:42.100
Just shut up and put someone else on the line!

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.060
Got it?!

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:43.770
'Kay...

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.610
She hung up!!!

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.290
What are you trying to achieve by doing all this?

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:55.660
I'm going to defeat No. 88 right in front of your eyes.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:57.900
Musubi-chan?

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:01.700
When I do, that weird girl will show up again.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:06.040
Losing like that...

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.350
Do you really think I'd let it go?

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.840
Ma-chan, pick up the phone.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:16.240
Kusano-tan. When you put the receiver down, you hang up.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.200
Hang up?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.760
They'll call back if you wait a bit.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:20.840
That's right.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:21.620
Again?

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:30.560
Kuu's phone!

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.000
Yes?

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.260
Doesn't sound like No. 88.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.750
Eighty eight?

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:37.330
Aww. Why can't it be me?

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.320
Anyone's fine, just put someone decent on the line.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.240
How rude.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.750
They hung up again!

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.940
I'll kill you!!!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.800
Goddammit!!!

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.150
It seems like I'll get this done faster if I use you.

00:16:59.150 --> 00:16:59.620
Eh?

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:03.240
Was it really a prank call?

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:03.740
Yeah.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.840
But the person who called said something about No. 88, right?

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.830
Persistent, aren't they?

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.250
I'll go get it.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:12.590
Hello-

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.830
Matsu-san!

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.560
Mina-tan?

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:16.310
Onii-chan?

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.200
D-Don't listen to her!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:21.940
You get it now, don't you?

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:24.460
Your Ashikabi is in my hands now.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:25.440
Who are you?

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:28.230
Are you after Musubi-tan?

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.290
Hurry up and put her on the line.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.160
If you don't, your Ashikabi's life might be in danger-

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:37.890
Hello?

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:39.800
What are you doing?!

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:42.840
I-It's broken...

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:46.580
Argh. Now I lost the phone number!

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:51.700
Listen, you...

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.510
Do you fully understand the situation you're in?

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:57.830
D-Did you think that I'd put the others in danger for me?!

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:02.100
That voice... It was most likely No. 105 Benitsubasa.

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:05.550
If I recall correctly, Benitsubasa is one of the Disciplinary Squad members.

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:08.480
Which means it's safe to guess that she wants revenge.

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:09.740
Revenge?

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.010
We're going to find out where they're keeping Mina-tan immediately.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:17.840
That sound...

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:23.100
Mina-tan's cellphone is out of reach.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:24.970
Can you find him?

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.080
I will. No matter what.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.980
However, the security's gotten tighter since the escape.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:36.820
No matter how fast I work, it's going to take at least twenty minutes to hack into MBI's observation satellite.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.380
Sahashi-san... was kidnapped?

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.130
Matsu's looking for him right now.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.590
What are you going to do?

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:46.700
Just sobering up.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:52.070
Well then...

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:53.260
What should I do?

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:56.480
You said something quite conceited earlier.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.790
You're actually scared, aren't you?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.280
Why don't you cry for help?

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.040
Y-You think I'm scared of you?

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:02.980
You guys really are annoying.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.330
Now that I think about it, isn't Haihane taking too long?

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:09.470
Jeez, everyone's annoying me today.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.370
The sound I heard through the phone...

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:17.200
It's probably...

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:28.410
I have to run away somehow.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:30.210
Run where?

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:34.100
Running around like a little rodent...

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.890
It's really annoying, you know?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.110
Bingo.

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:46.790
Ka-Kazehana-san!

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.690
What do you think you're doing, showing up suddenly like that?

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:01.300
This is the legendary Flower Cup Sake.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:02.900
Um... Where did you find that?

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.410
This warehouse stores lots of famous sake.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.660
A-And she's drinking it, too...

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.140
You really know how to choose nice places, don't you?

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.060
You...!

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.260
You want a piece of me?

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:25.010
Yup. It's not logical.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:27.410
So annoying. I'll kill you in an instant.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.570
Ka-Kazehana-san!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.510
Haihane! You're slow!

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.300
I went to ask someone to reserve the video for me.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:37.470
You little...!

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.000
Well then...

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.730
What shall we do?

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.370
Onii-chan's so slow.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.060
Do you think something happened?

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:53.680
He's just late.

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:57.890
It's not like he's involved in The Sekirei Project like us.

00:20:58.310 --> 00:20:59.180
That's right.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:07.730
Minato...

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.980
Where's Minato?!

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:18.870
Today's curry rice. Minato-san will love it. I'm sure of it.

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:22.060
Onii-chan...

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:28.420
Kazehana-san, run away!

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:34.830
What'll you do?

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:38.640
First of all, should we cut off his head?

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.480
Looks like things are getting quite interesting.

